# d8g_genmesh_PROLOGUE_REPAIR.diff
#
#   THE FROZEN d8g_genmesh.sh (md5 5b9db5102a4ffe04abffec6f7648d0c1, frozen
#   075f6edf6) GENERATES A cmd.sh THAT ABORTS AT ITS SECOND LINE.  Lines
#   232-233 emit
#       set -e
#       source /home/dafoamuser/dafoam/loadDAFoam.sh
#   and that order exits rc=1 inside OpenFOAM's own etc/bashrc.  `cd` on the
#   next line, and every step after it, NEVER RUNS.
#
#   THE FROZEN FILE IS NOT EDITED.  This diff is against a candidate,
#   d8g_genmesh_candidate.sh (md5 2b22d01e265ba8362a12644c32bbd409).  The
#   amendment and the re-freeze are the dafoam-supervisor's acts.
#
#   ONE HUNK.  NOTHING ELSE IS TOUCHED: not the registered level table, not
#   C0_QUADS / WANT_QUADS / WANT_POINTS, not G-GEN.1's run-root refusal, not
#   G-GEN.2's c0 discriminating assertion, not G-GEN.3's exact-4.0 coarsening
#   ratio, not G-GEN.4's digest pin, not G-GEN.5's rc test, not the 3,600 s
#   containment deadline, not the two checkMesh runs, not the post-run chown.
#
#   THAT SCOPE CLAIM IS MEASURED, NOT ASSERTED.  Comparing the two files with
#   all comment and blank lines stripped -- so only executable shell is
#   compared -- gives EXACTLY ONE REMOVED LINE (`set -e`, the one that was
#   ahead of the source) and EIGHT ADDED (the assertion, and `set -e`
#   reinstated behind it).  The `source` line itself is NOT removed and NOT
#   moved.  Nothing else in 411 lines differs.
#   *** AND A NOTE ON HOW THAT NUMBER WAS ARRIVED AT, BECAUSE MY FIRST ATTEMPT
#   WAS WRONG.  A grep-based scope check over the registered keys reported the
#   two files as DIFFERENT, and the cause was that the new COMMENT BLOCK quotes
#   `3600`, `G-GEN.5` and the image digest while EXPLAINING them.  The checker
#   was matching the repair's own prose and calling it a change to the thing
#   the prose was about.  The executable-line diff is the check that actually
#   answers the question.  A SCOPE CHECK THAT CANNOT TELL A CITATION FROM A
#   CHANGE IS NOT A SCOPE CHECK -- and it failed in the direction that would
#   have had me report a false difference, not a false sameness. ***
#
# OBSERVED, NOT INFERRED
#   Measured on D8G's OWN pinned image
#   sha256:2927768a16acdea0330180fff95c8879c1dda9efcf6028728523b7dee30f6d35
#   -- NOT the A3GC image; D8G pins `dafoam-idwarp-rot`, a different image, and
#   an earlier reading of this defect was taken on the wrong one --
#   at D8G's OWN `--user 0:0`, under D8G's OWN nesting
#   `bash -lc "timeout -k 60 3600 bash cmd.sh"`, with lines 232-233 copied
#   VERBATIM from the frozen file:
#       OpenFOAM-v2506/etc/config.sh/setup: line 207:
#       pop_var_context: head of shell_variables not a function context
#       rc = 1, line 3 NEVER REACHED.
#   Control, `set -e` removed from the same file: line 3 reached, rc = 0.
#   The abort is inside OpenFOAM's own etc/bashrc, is INDEPENDENT OF uid (it
#   reproduces at uid 0 and at uid 1002) and happens under both `bash -c` and
#   `bash -lc`.
#   STILL NOT OBSERVED, AND SAID PLAINLY: d8g_genmesh.sh has not been run end
#   to end, so the abort has been observed on THE GENERATED COMMAND rather than
#   on the script as a whole.  What is observed is the exact two lines this
#   file emits, at its uid, in its image, under its nesting.
#
# THE HUNK
#
# (a) *** THE ORDER IS REVERSED, AND `set -e` IS NOT MERELY MOVED -- IT IS
#     MOVED BEHIND A TEST, BECAUSE THE OBVIOUS REPAIR IS ALSO WRONG. ***
#     Simply deleting `set -e` would "work" and would be a defect: WITHOUT
#     `set -e` this source returns rc 0 EVEN WHEN THE ENVIRONMENT DID NOT LOAD
#     (measured: rc 0, WM_PROJECT_DIR empty, cgns_utils absent).  A SILENT
#     SUCCESS AND A SILENT FAILURE CARRY THE SAME rc, so rc cannot be the test.
#     The source is therefore checked by a POSITIVE CAPABILITY ASSERTION --
#     demand the environment SHOW `WM_PROJECT_DIR` and `cgns_utils`, which
#     exist only after a successful load, and exit 97 naming both plus `id` if
#     it cannot.  CLAUDE.md rule 3, plant the zero, applied to an environment
#     instead of a field.  `set -e` is armed immediately AFTER the assertion,
#     where it can still do its job for every step that follows.
#     PLANTED CONTROL, MEASURED ON THE GENERATED FILE ITSELF, so the assertion
#     is shown able to fail and not merely able to pass:
#       --user 0:0    -> reaches past the prologue, `cgns_utils` usable, rc 0
#       --user 1000:1000 -> "Permission denied", ABORT G-GEN.0,
#                        WM_PROJECT_DIR=[], cgns_utils=MISSING, rc 97
#
# (b) *** THE ESCAPING IS PART OF THE REPAIR, NOT COSMETIC. ***
#     This heredoc is UNQUOTED (`<<CMDEOF`), so every `$` is expanded BY THE
#     HOST SHELL as the file is written.  An unescaped `${WM_PROJECT_DIR:-}`
#     would have been expanded on the host -- to the EMPTY STRING -- and the
#     assertion would have been written into cmd.sh as `[ -z "" ]`, i.e. it
#     would have ABORTED EVERY RUN WHILE APPEARING TO TEST THE ENVIRONMENT.
#     That is the same failure shape as the defect being repaired: an
#     instrument reporting about something it is not testing.  Every `$` that
#     must survive to the container is backslash-escaped, exactly as this
#     file's existing `\$(id -u)` and `\$(seq 1 $NC)` already are.
#     VERIFIED BY EXTRACTION, NOT BY READING: the heredoc was executed in
#     isolation with dummy registered values and the emitted cmd.sh was read
#     back -- it carries the LITERAL `${WM_PROJECT_DIR:-}`, `$(command -v
#     cgns_utils || echo MISSING)` and `$(id)`, while `$LEVEL` correctly
#     expanded on the host to `cd /mnt/mesh_build_L3`.  Nothing under
#     /home/ubuntu/certonomous-runs was created to check this.
#
# THE ASYMMETRY WITH A3GC, WHICH IS THE POINT WORTH KEEPING
#   A3GC's generator carried the SAME CLASS of defect -- a mishandled
#   environment load in a container prologue -- and the two rungs fail in
#   OPPOSITE ways:
#     D8G  wrapped nothing, so the abort propagates: :299 `test "$GRC" -eq 0`
#          fires `ABORT G-GEN.5 generation rc=1` and THE RUNG STOPS.
#     A3GC wrapped the source in `>/dev/null 2>&1 || true`, so the same class
#          of failure was SWALLOWED and the rung went on to run SEVEN DEAD
#          STEPS, reporting `cgns_utils: command not found` -- a missing
#          binary -- instead of a dead environment.
#   That is the difference between a rung that stopped and a rung that ran
#   seven dead steps, and it is entirely attributable to the `|| true`.
#   D8G's loudness is the reason this defect is a repair and not an incident.
#
# NOT DONE
#   D8G's run root /home/ubuntu/certonomous-runs/CURRICULUM-D8G-a6-grid-triple
#   is NOT created by this diff and still reads ABSENT.  Generation under it is
#   the supervisor's call and is not taken here.
#

--- d8g_genmesh.sh	2026-09-11 17:40:03.973900134 +0000
+++ d8g_genmesh_candidate.sh	2026-09-11 18:32:22.571314779 +0000
@@ -228,9 +228,55 @@
                   "coords_sha_free": True}, sort_keys=True))
 PYEOF
 
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# THE PROLOGUE ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING AND WAS MEASURED, NOT REASONED.
+#
+# This file previously opened cmd.sh with
+#     set -e
+#     source /home/dafoamuser/dafoam/loadDAFoam.sh
+# and THAT ORDER ABORTS.  Measured on D8G's OWN pinned image
+# (sha256:2927768a16acdea0330180fff95c8879c1dda9efcf6028728523b7dee30f6d35),
+# at D8G's OWN --user 0:0, under D8G's OWN nesting
+# (bash -lc "timeout -k 60 3600 bash cmd.sh"):
+#     OpenFOAM-v2506/etc/config.sh/setup: line 207:
+#     pop_var_context: head of shell_variables not a function context
+#   -> the shell exits rc=1 AT LINE 2 and `cd` -- and every line after it --
+#      NEVER RUNS.  Control, `set -e` removed: line 3 runs, rc 0.
+# The abort is inside OpenFOAM's own etc/bashrc, is independent of uid, and
+# happens under both `bash -c` and `bash -lc`.
+#
+# *** D8G FAILS LOUDLY, AND THAT IS THE ONE MERCY HERE.  Line :299 below tests
+#     `test "$GRC" -eq 0` and aborts G-GEN.5 with the rc.  The sister defect in
+#     A3GC's generator wrapped the same source in `>/dev/null 2>&1 || true`, so
+#     A3GC went on to run SEVEN dead steps and reported a missing binary
+#     instead of a dead environment.  Same class, opposite failure mode: THIS
+#     rung stops; THAT rung continued. ***
+#
+# `set -e` is therefore armed AFTER the source, and the source is checked by a
+# POSITIVE CAPABILITY ASSERTION rather than by its rc -- because its rc is not
+# a test: WITHOUT `set -e` this source returns rc 0 EVEN WHEN THE ENVIRONMENT
+# DID NOT LOAD (measured: rc 0, WM_PROJECT_DIR empty, cgns_utils absent).  A
+# silent success and a silent failure carry the same rc.  The assertion demands
+# the environment SHOW a variable and a binary that exist only after a
+# successful load (CLAUDE.md rule 3 -- plant the zero -- applied to an
+# environment rather than a field).
+#
+# NOTE THE ESCAPING.  This heredoc is UNQUOTED (<<CMDEOF), so every `$`
+# below that must survive to the CONTAINER is backslash-escaped, exactly as the
+# existing `\$(id -u)` and `\$(seq 1 $NC)` are.  An unescaped ${WM_PROJECT_DIR}
+# here would be expanded by the HOST shell -- to the empty string -- and the
+# assertion would then test nothing at all.
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 cat > "$BUILD/cmd.sh" <<CMDEOF
-set -e
 source /home/dafoamuser/dafoam/loadDAFoam.sh
+if [ -z "\${WM_PROJECT_DIR:-}" ] || ! command -v cgns_utils >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+  printf 'ABORT G-GEN.0 loadDAFoam.sh did not populate the environment.\n' >&2
+  printf '  WM_PROJECT_DIR = [%s]\n' "\${WM_PROJECT_DIR:-}" >&2
+  printf '  cgns_utils     = %s\n' "\$(command -v cgns_utils || echo MISSING)" >&2
+  printf '  id             = %s\n' "\$(id)" >&2
+  exit 97
+fi
+set -e
 cd /mnt/mesh_build_$LEVEL
 echo D8G_GENMESH_UID: \$(id -u)
 tar -xvf CRM_surfMesh.cgns.tar.gz
